WEBVTT


00:00:40.321 --> 00:00:42.455
You
got 20 minutes.


00:01:19.594 --> 00:01:25.565
<i>♪ To get inside my mind Is
this what you wanted</i>


00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:29.936
<i>♪ Get me all turned
around Tell me baby</i>


00:01:40.881 --> 00:01:42.882
Hello?


00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:23.516
No! No!


00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.778
What's
going on in there?


00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:02.848
John own memories are
intruding. He's
having a seizure.


00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.018
Marjorie! Get in there! Now!


00:05:35.415 --> 00:05:38.284
<i>Senator
Rockford has been identified
as the target...</i>


00:05:38.286 --> 00:05:41.487
<i>of an FBI investigation,
involving embezzlement and
accusations of blackmail.</i>


00:05:41.489 --> 00:05:43.422
Senator!


00:05:43.424 --> 00:05:48.127
I wholeheartedly and
emphatically deny any and all
allegations leveled against me.


00:05:48.129 --> 00:05:51.197
<i>His attorney
has secured the services
of Mindscape...</i>


00:05:51.199 --> 00:05:53.499
the world's top memory
detective agency...


00:05:53.501 --> 00:05:57.870
<i>to gather information about his
past and help the FBI with
the investigation.</i>


00:05:57.872 --> 00:06:00.272
<i>Memory detectives, as they're
commonly known...</i>


00:06:00.274 --> 00:06:02.808
<i>have experienced a resurgence
in recent years...</i>


00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:07.046
<i>thanks to the growing number of
cases solved using the remote
viewing technique.</i>


00:06:07.048 --> 00:06:10.449
<i>In the early 70 s, the Defense
Intelligence Agency</i>


00:06:10.451 --> 00:06:14.787
<i>began conducting top secret
experiments with people with
psychic abilities</i>


00:06:14.789 --> 00:06:18.557
<i>to help gather intelligence
for modern warfare.</i>


00:06:18.559 --> 00:06:20.926
<i>They came across a
group of ESP's...</i>


00:06:20.928 --> 00:06:23.329
<i>that had the ability to access
people's memories</i>


00:06:23.331 --> 00:06:27.833
<i>and observe them as they were
experienced in the past
by the subjects.</i>


00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.472
<i>The findings of memory
detectives do not yet carry
the same weight...</i>


00:06:33.474 --> 00:06:35.041
<i>as DNA evidence in court...</i>


00:06:35.043 --> 00:06:38.644
<i>but currently prove more
reliable than polygraph tests.</i>


00:06:38.646 --> 00:06:41.881
<i>They say, remote viewing is
nothing more than an
elaborate scam...</i>


00:06:41.883 --> 00:06:45.384
<i>but the reality is, remote
viewers have been
solving cases...</i>


00:06:45.386 --> 00:06:47.386
<i>that have been cold for years.</i>


00:06:47.388 --> 00:06:50.623
<i>Most recently, the murder of
child actress Kate Henderson...</i>


00:06:50.625 --> 00:06:52.758
<i>was solved by memory
detective John Washington.</i>


00:06:55.862 --> 00:06:57.696
Shit.


00:07:03.203 --> 00:07:04.670
Hello?


00:07:04.672 --> 00:07:06.038
<i>CALLER Ah, hello!
Good Morning!</i>


00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.940
I'm calling about the
house for sale.


00:07:07.942 --> 00:07:12.344
No... no... we're not selling
the house anymore, I'm sorry.


00:07:12.346 --> 00:07:15.214
Well... the agency listing says
it's still active.


00:07:15.216 --> 00:07:18.317
Yeah, I know it's still listed
at the agency, but we're not
selling it, okay?


00:07:18.319 --> 00:07:20.152
Mr. Washington's own
traumatic memories...


00:07:20.154 --> 00:07:22.088
<i>were blending in with his
clients memories...</i>


00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:23.389
<i>which impaired his ability to
focus during sessions.</i>


00:07:23.391 --> 00:07:25.558
And thank you.


00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:29.862
<i>Now it seems, Senator Rockford
is betting his political
career on Mindscape...</i>


00:07:29.864 --> 00:07:34.533
<i>the prime memory detective
agency in the world.</i>


00:07:34.535 --> 00:07:40.072
<i>The rumors that the Mindscape
program is dangerous,
are unfounded.</i>


00:07:58.792 --> 00:08:00.292
John is here.


00:08:00.294 --> 00:08:04.497
John... how are you?


00:08:04.499 --> 00:08:06.932
I'm great.


00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:08.601
You're still taking
the medication?


00:08:08.603 --> 00:08:09.969
No, I'm done with all that.


00:08:09.971 --> 00:08:12.805
Well, you're lucky the
stroke was mild.


00:08:12.807 --> 00:08:16.242
You could be relearning your
abc's right now.


00:08:16.244 --> 00:08:19.145
That's true.


00:08:19.147 --> 00:08:20.379
Yes?


00:08:20.381 --> 00:08:23.382
Uh... I'm good.


00:08:23.384 --> 00:08:25.451
Nice.


00:08:28.788 --> 00:08:31.857
You met anybody recently?


00:08:31.859 --> 00:08:34.860
You know, John, maybe it's time
to get back in the running.


00:08:34.862 --> 00:08:36.395
I'm not there yet.


00:08:36.397 --> 00:08:37.730
It's been two years.


00:08:37.732 --> 00:08:40.099
You should move on from what
happened to your wife.


00:08:41.902 --> 00:08:44.236
And you know it
wasn't your fault.


00:08:44.238 --> 00:08:45.771
Yeah, well...


00:08:45.773 --> 00:08:48.607
Oh, shit!
Shit! Sorry.


00:08:48.609 --> 00:08:50.609
Ah, don't worry about it.
Don't worry!


00:08:50.611 --> 00:08:52.178
I'm so sorry. Don't
worry about it.


00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.812
I'm sorry.


00:08:53.814 --> 00:08:57.183
Here... sit down! Sorry.


00:08:57.185 --> 00:08:59.585
I heard Senator Rockford on...
TV...


00:08:59.587 --> 00:09:03.222
talking about the possibility
of hiring a memory detective.


00:09:03.224 --> 00:09:07.626
Oh, yeah, yeah. Peter Lundgren
is already working on the case.


00:09:07.628 --> 00:09:10.029
Rockford hired him. Lundgren?


00:09:10.031 --> 00:09:13.232
C mon! I was better than him
on my worst day!


00:09:13.234 --> 00:09:15.834
Yeah, but gifts like yours
need to be used.


00:09:15.836 --> 00:09:17.403
You've been out of the
game for months.


00:09:17.405 --> 00:09:20.806
And Lundgrens' success nowadays
is close to 100 percent.


00:09:24.678 --> 00:09:26.145
What's the matter?


00:09:30.317 --> 00:09:32.985
To be honest, I'm
running out of money.


00:09:34.854 --> 00:09:37.523
You still have the beach house?


00:09:37.525 --> 00:09:38.624
Yeah.


00:09:38.626 --> 00:09:39.959
Go ahead. Sell it.


00:09:39.961 --> 00:09:44.430
I'm not ready to sell it yet.


00:09:44.432 --> 00:09:48.367
What I was wondering was
whether I could do
something for Mindscape.


00:09:48.369 --> 00:09:52.071
As it happens, I, uh...


00:09:52.073 --> 00:09:55.407
I might have something you're
right for, perfect actually.


00:09:55.409 --> 00:09:58.677
Her name is Anna.


00:09:58.679 --> 00:10:01.647
Oh, you're kidding.


00:10:01.649 --> 00:10:05.251
Forget about the name, right?


00:10:05.253 --> 00:10:08.587
She used to be my patient
when she was little.


00:10:08.589 --> 00:10:10.556
Very special girl...


00:10:10.558 --> 00:10:14.827
she's a teenager now, but I
don't think a... a
doctor can help.


00:10:14.829 --> 00:10:16.829
Maybe a viewer can.


00:10:16.831 --> 00:10:18.497
Well, what's her problem?


00:10:18.499 --> 00:10:22.167
She's on a hunger strike. All
you have to do is
get her to eat.


00:10:22.169 --> 00:10:24.770
Just tell the parents to hide
the fashion magazines.


00:10:24.772 --> 00:10:28.474
John...


00:10:28.476 --> 00:10:32.544
You know, it could be a quick
one for you, if you didn't
wanna sell the beach house.


00:10:49.597 --> 00:10:53.032
<i>Hi
John, I'm so happy you're
back in the saddle.</i>


00:10:53.034 --> 00:10:56.135
<i>Anna's still refusing to eat,
trying to pressure them...</i>


00:10:56.137 --> 00:10:58.237
into letting her out
of the house.


00:10:58.239 --> 00:11:02.341
She's very fragile, so
tread carefully.


00:11:02.343 --> 00:11:06.912
<i>Try to find a trauma for her
therapist to work on... bye.</i>


00:12:21.087 --> 00:12:24.156
Thank you so much for
working on Anna's case.


00:12:24.158 --> 00:12:26.392
I'm Michelle. John.


00:12:26.394 --> 00:12:29.895
And this is Anna's stepfather,
Robert.


00:12:29.897 --> 00:12:32.598
Sebastian speaks very
highly of you.


00:12:34.968 --> 00:12:38.003
Even as a baby, Anna
was unusual.


00:12:38.005 --> 00:12:42.307
She didn't smile when you
smiled at her, but she didn't
cry much, either.


00:12:42.309 --> 00:12:47.479
I would say she was unusually
focused for a child,
always calm.


00:12:47.481 --> 00:12:50.816
She looked at things as if she
already knew what they were.


00:12:50.818 --> 00:12:56.789
Later, of course, we took her
to a specialist, and her IQ
score came back off the charts.


00:12:56.791 --> 00:12:59.024
When was the last time she ate?


00:12:59.026 --> 00:13:00.793
She stopped eating one week ago.


00:13:00.795 --> 00:13:04.930
She's taking vitamins and
drinking water, but
nothing else.


00:13:04.932 --> 00:13:10.269
In my opinion, she should be...
in a place that can provide
the proper care.


00:13:10.271 --> 00:13:13.439
I'm sure Anna can get
better here.


00:13:13.441 --> 00:13:16.308
Mr. Washington, ah... as I'm
sure you can appreciate...


00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.944
this is a matter that requires
great discretion.


00:13:18.946 --> 00:13:21.246
I will need you to sign a
non-disclosure contract...


00:13:21.248 --> 00:13:26.385
that anything revealed in
Anna's memories can't be
disseminated beyond
Michelle and myself.


00:13:26.387 --> 00:13:27.719
Of course.


00:13:27.721 --> 00:13:32.424
Anna is so special, she's so
many talents, she's...


00:13:34.661 --> 00:13:36.462
Gifted.


00:13:36.464 --> 00:13:38.397
Yes, gifted.


00:13:39.999 --> 00:13:42.367
I think there are
better words for it.


00:13:42.369 --> 00:13:44.436
Such as?


00:13:44.438 --> 00:13:47.072
I would say haunted.


00:13:52.245 --> 00:13:54.880
What happened to
Anna's real father?


00:13:54.882 --> 00:13:57.749
He died... when I was pregnant.


00:13:57.751 --> 00:13:58.851
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:13:58.853 --> 00:14:00.819
Does Anna get along with Robert?


00:14:00.821 --> 00:14:04.923
Not well, lately... but he's
tried to do his best for her.


00:14:04.925 --> 00:14:07.793
I see. This way.


00:14:07.795 --> 00:14:11.797
Is there any specific reason
why Anna is refusing to eat?


00:14:11.799 --> 00:14:14.233
She wants to go back to school,
but that's impossible.


00:14:14.235 --> 00:14:17.503
I'm sure Sebastian told you
about her cutting herself.


00:14:17.505 --> 00:14:20.572
We've had to remove all sharp
objects from her room.


00:14:20.574 --> 00:14:22.574
We need to protect her.


00:14:22.576 --> 00:14:25.844
From what?


00:14:25.846 --> 00:14:28.647
To protect her, from herself.


00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.302
Sweetie. This is John...


00:14:50.304 --> 00:14:52.938
the gentleman I told you was
coming to visit.


00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.774
Aren't you late for your
AA meeting, Mom?


00:15:12.892 --> 00:15:14.760
Can I have a seat? Can
I have a seat?


00:15:17.797 --> 00:15:20.032
Do you mind? Do you mind?


00:15:20.034 --> 00:15:24.269
We won't guess the next one for
sure, so go ahead, make
yourself comfortable.


00:15:28.207 --> 00:15:30.876
That's quite the party
trick you have there.


00:15:45.692 --> 00:15:48.660
What's the metronome for?


00:15:48.662 --> 00:15:51.830
I like the rhythm when I draw.
It's soothing.


00:15:58.805 --> 00:16:00.472
Better?


00:16:00.474 --> 00:16:01.840
Much.


00:16:06.145 --> 00:16:09.214
Anna, you know what
catabolysis is?


00:16:09.216 --> 00:16:11.416
If you don't eat, your
organs are gonna fail.


00:16:11.418 --> 00:16:14.086
John, do you know what "prana"
is?


00:16:14.088 --> 00:16:17.289
It's sanskrit, it
means vital life.


00:16:17.291 --> 00:16:19.491
There are Yogis in India
who rarely eat.


00:16:19.493 --> 00:16:22.995
They get all their energy or
"prana" from the air
and the sun.


00:16:22.997 --> 00:16:24.830
Is that what you're doing?


00:16:24.832 --> 00:16:26.198
Are you a doctor?


00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.867
No, but I do have to ask
you some questions.


00:16:34.273 --> 00:16:39.678
I would like you to tell me
what expression you see.


00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:44.650
What am I getting in exchange
for making you earn some of
Robert's money?


00:16:44.652 --> 00:16:47.753
Well, you might get to know
yourself better.


00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.760
What do you see?


00:16:58.498 --> 00:17:00.899
Malice.


00:17:04.237 --> 00:17:06.638
I'm kidding.


00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:09.341
He's expressing happiness,
maybe even affection.


00:17:12.111 --> 00:17:13.945
What about this guy?


00:17:15.915 --> 00:17:18.050
That guy's pissed off.


00:17:18.052 --> 00:17:19.851
Uh-huh.


00:17:21.954 --> 00:17:24.423
What about her?


00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.362
I think her husband's out late,
and she's wondering
where he is.


00:17:30.364 --> 00:17:34.199
She's worried he's with someone
else, but she's also glad to
have the down time...


00:17:34.201 --> 00:17:36.368
'cause he's a loser.


00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.774
Right.


00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.712
I'm gonna tell you a story...


00:17:46.714 --> 00:17:50.582
and then I'm gonna ask you
a question. Okay?


00:17:52.919 --> 00:17:56.488
There's this girl about your
age at her mother's funeral.


00:17:56.490 --> 00:18:00.792
At the funeral, she sees this
guy she's never seen before.


00:18:00.794 --> 00:18:02.694
She gets to meet him, briefly.


00:18:02.696 --> 00:18:06.298
And she thinks he's amazing.
He's everything she's
ever wanted.


00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:09.334
She falls in love with him,
right there and then.


00:18:09.336 --> 00:18:12.704
But, in the crowds at the
funeral, she gets separated...


00:18:12.706 --> 00:18:17.442
from him before she has a
chance to ask for his number.


00:18:17.444 --> 00:18:21.813
And two days later... this
girl... kills her own sister.


00:18:23.616 --> 00:18:26.451
What's her motive for
killing her sister?


00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:34.326
Her motive is she wants to
meet the guy again.


00:18:38.464 --> 00:18:40.632
Did I get it right?


00:18:40.634 --> 00:18:44.770
Huh? Oh, there's no
right answer.


00:18:47.406 --> 00:18:49.841
Depends on what
you're looking for.


00:18:49.843 --> 00:18:51.643
Why is that?


00:18:51.645 --> 00:18:55.881
You're testing me to see if I
think like a sociopath.


00:18:55.883 --> 00:18:59.117
Sociopaths sometimes have
trouble reading
facial expressions.


00:18:59.119 --> 00:19:02.387
With the second test, I gave
you the answer you were
looking for...


00:19:02.389 --> 00:19:05.123
but, the fact is, that story
has a flawed set up.


00:19:05.125 --> 00:19:08.059
The more logical outcome would
be for the girl to
kill her father.


00:19:09.829 --> 00:19:12.731
Why?


00:19:12.733 --> 00:19:15.967
If the girl didn't know the
man, it's unlikely her
sister would.


00:19:15.969 --> 00:19:19.504
And it was her mother's funeral
where she met this guy...


00:19:19.506 --> 00:19:21.206
so it would make more sense for
her to kill her father.


00:19:21.208 --> 00:19:24.042
There would be a higher
probability that the...


00:19:24.044 --> 00:19:27.712
the mystery stud would attend
her father's funeral.


00:19:30.449 --> 00:19:32.751
That's probably true.


00:19:32.753 --> 00:19:36.121
I'm not a sociopath, just smart
enough to think like one.


00:19:42.461 --> 00:19:44.830
Can I see what you're drawing?


00:19:55.208 --> 00:19:58.710
If you're not a doctor,
then what are you?


00:19:58.712 --> 00:20:02.581
I take people to their memories.


00:20:12.124 --> 00:20:13.692
She's monitored all the time?


00:20:13.694 --> 00:20:15.961
24-7.


00:20:15.963 --> 00:20:20.165
If you need anything while
you're here, you can ask me or
Ralph, we both watch Anna.


00:20:20.167 --> 00:20:21.466
I'm John.


00:20:21.468 --> 00:20:24.736
Oh, I'm Judith...
this is my cell.


00:20:24.738 --> 00:20:28.073
Call me, if you can't
make a session.


00:20:28.075 --> 00:20:29.674
I will.


00:20:38.584 --> 00:20:41.052
You were right about her,
she's smart.


00:20:41.054 --> 00:20:44.422
Special kid, lots of problems.


00:20:44.424 --> 00:20:48.159
What do you think are the
underlying issues?


00:20:48.161 --> 00:20:52.864
Depression, bipolar disorder
with deep-seeded narcissism.


00:20:52.866 --> 00:20:56.935
I'm gonna need her full file to
know what memories to target.


00:20:56.937 --> 00:20:59.337
Parents don't want
full disclosure.


00:20:59.339 --> 00:21:01.873
What? Why? I signed
an agreement!


00:21:01.875 --> 00:21:05.410
She's been in and out of
boarding schools, involved in
some incidents...


00:21:05.412 --> 00:21:07.412
but you don't need to
get into that.


00:21:07.414 --> 00:21:09.581
Just let her take the lead,
you know?


00:21:09.583 --> 00:21:13.184
I mean... a few memories where
the parents screw up.


00:21:13.186 --> 00:21:17.756
As you know, usually, the
dramatic experience of actually
going back into memories...


00:21:17.758 --> 00:21:22.360
affects people, gives them
perspective on their
present lives...


00:21:22.362 --> 00:21:25.664
to stop overeating, stop
smoking... whatever.


00:21:25.666 --> 00:21:28.767
Make her eat. Simple case.


00:21:39.078 --> 00:21:40.745
Will I know I'm in a memory?


00:21:40.747 --> 00:21:43.949
It should feel like it's
happening for the first time...


00:21:43.951 --> 00:21:47.319
but it'll be different from
the original event.


00:21:47.321 --> 00:21:52.023
Because your unconscious mind
will know that you've
been there before.


00:21:52.025 --> 00:21:53.925
Also...


00:21:53.927 --> 00:21:56.995
me being there makes
it different.


00:21:58.597 --> 00:22:02.801
The equipment is useful to
record the session.


00:22:14.613 --> 00:22:17.015
I will be watching you for
the whole time.


00:22:17.017 --> 00:22:21.386
If anything happens, I can
bring you back, right away.
Okay?


00:22:21.388 --> 00:22:25.256
Now, you may see me in the
distance, but you won't
know that it's me.


00:22:25.258 --> 00:22:29.094
If I'm next to you, you won't
be able to see me at all...


00:22:29.096 --> 00:22:30.362
unless I call you back.


00:22:30.364 --> 00:22:32.330
Understand?


00:22:32.332 --> 00:22:34.532
Yes.


00:22:34.534 --> 00:22:37.669
Please put these in your ears.


00:22:37.671 --> 00:22:41.006
They conceal a tone, hidden
in white noise.


00:22:41.008 --> 00:22:43.775
It enables the brain to go
into a theta state.


00:22:43.777 --> 00:22:45.977
Can we use my metronome.
As well?


00:22:45.979 --> 00:22:48.079
Uh... sure.


00:22:53.919 --> 00:22:56.187
Where are we going?


00:22:56.189 --> 00:22:57.922
Focus on your first memory.


00:22:57.924 --> 00:23:00.091
The further back we can go,
the better.


00:23:02.361 --> 00:23:04.229
Give me your hands.


00:23:07.733 --> 00:23:09.667
Relax.


00:23:10.503 --> 00:23:13.371
Think about that first memory.


00:23:13.373 --> 00:23:16.808
At first, your memories will
jump around, but that's okay.


00:23:26.519 --> 00:23:28.453
When you're ready...


00:23:28.455 --> 00:23:29.754
close your eyes.


00:23:48.274 --> 00:23:51.276
Let's begin...


00:23:57.450 --> 00:23:58.817
now.


00:23:58.819 --> 00:24:00.752
I like you being here with us...


00:24:00.754 --> 00:24:03.021
We all know you like girls.


00:24:05.458 --> 00:24:07.625
She's just a girl for god sakes!


00:24:07.627 --> 00:24:09.127
We have a responsibility!


00:24:09.129 --> 00:24:10.361
Let me out!


00:24:10.363 --> 00:24:12.697
She needs to be in an
institution!


00:24:12.699 --> 00:24:14.999
She's my daughter!


00:24:19.805 --> 00:24:23.575
This old man, he played three.


00:24:23.577 --> 00:24:26.744
He played
knick-knack on my knee.


00:24:26.746 --> 00:24:29.047
With a knick-knack
paddy whack...


00:24:29.049 --> 00:24:30.782
give a dog a bone...


00:24:30.784 --> 00:24:34.752
this old man
came rolling home.


00:24:52.471 --> 00:24:54.672
What game are you playing,
honey?


00:24:54.674 --> 00:24:57.008
Can I play with you?


00:25:00.813 --> 00:25:03.047
You have to be quiet.


00:25:06.785 --> 00:25:08.987
What are you up to?


00:25:12.792 --> 00:25:15.727
Mommy's not feeling well today.


00:25:15.729 --> 00:25:17.962
You can't do that! You
can't just...


00:25:17.964 --> 00:25:20.932
We have to think about Anna.
Anna is the focus of
the attention.


00:25:20.934 --> 00:25:22.734
Don't you think I'm
thinking about her?


00:25:22.736 --> 00:25:25.403
We have a responsibility! We
are not the right people!


00:25:25.405 --> 00:25:27.705
This is not the place for her,
Michelle!


00:25:40.986 --> 00:25:44.355
Come with me, young lady! Dad!
Let me down!


00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:50.962
I'll let you out when you
realize that spying on
people is wrong.


00:25:50.964 --> 00:25:52.664
For god's sakes,
She's only a girl!


00:25:52.666 --> 00:25:54.432
She's different, Michelle.


00:25:54.434 --> 00:25:58.236
She's not like other children,
she needs to be in an
institution.


00:26:02.408 --> 00:26:05.610
Well, why isn't it here, then?
Because I put it in here.


00:26:08.415 --> 00:26:10.215
She's my daughter.


00:26:10.217 --> 00:26:13.585
She tried to stab you, for
Christ's sakes!


00:26:13.587 --> 00:26:15.053
Mom!


00:26:18.324 --> 00:26:21.459
And coming back... now.


00:26:24.297 --> 00:26:26.164
Ow.


00:26:26.166 --> 00:26:28.333
Are you okay?


00:26:28.335 --> 00:26:29.834
You were there?


00:26:29.836 --> 00:26:32.003
I was right next to you.


00:26:32.005 --> 00:26:34.806
Spooky.


00:26:36.242 --> 00:26:37.675
Can we do more?


00:26:37.677 --> 00:26:39.277
Next time.


00:26:45.251 --> 00:26:50.989
Self-involved, emotionally
stunted retards is what one
hopes for in parents.


00:26:50.991 --> 00:26:53.291
Did you see the letter opener?


00:26:53.293 --> 00:26:55.393
I did.


00:26:55.395 --> 00:26:59.063
Maybe my stepdad is the one you
should be testing for
personality disorders.


00:26:59.065 --> 00:27:01.933
Is he why you're on a
hunger strike?


00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:10.341
So you married?


00:27:10.343 --> 00:27:12.543
I was.


00:27:12.545 --> 00:27:15.113
What was her name?


00:27:15.115 --> 00:27:16.347
Same as yours.


00:27:19.251 --> 00:27:21.319
I like her already.


00:27:23.689 --> 00:27:25.023
Show me a picture.


00:27:25.025 --> 00:27:27.492
I don't carry one anymore.


00:27:27.494 --> 00:27:29.761
C'mon, John.


00:27:29.763 --> 00:27:33.064
A guy like you always has a
picture in his wallet.


00:27:33.066 --> 00:27:35.066
I'll show you a picture...


00:27:35.068 --> 00:27:37.302
if you agree to eat something.


00:27:41.373 --> 00:27:44.275
You wanna see her?


00:27:44.277 --> 00:27:46.411
It's up to you.


00:27:54.853 --> 00:27:56.587
Robert desperately wants
to put me away.


00:27:56.589 --> 00:28:00.258
And something like LSD in my
food would make me act crazy.


00:28:01.794 --> 00:28:04.329
Well then, let's flip
out together.


00:28:04.331 --> 00:28:06.464
If I start hallucinating,
you'll demand a drug test...


00:28:06.466 --> 00:28:08.966
before they lock me away in a
padded room, right?


00:28:08.968 --> 00:28:11.436
I swear.


00:28:11.438 --> 00:28:13.171
C mon, let's eat!


00:28:27.252 --> 00:28:29.220
She's pretty.


00:28:38.364 --> 00:28:41.833
<i>Eat slowly so you don't
make yourself sick.</i>


00:28:45.771 --> 00:28:51.042
Why do you wanna see this
antique letter opener?


00:28:51.044 --> 00:28:54.645
I like to confirm memories,
just to be sure.


00:28:54.647 --> 00:28:57.048
I cut her accidentally.


00:28:57.883 --> 00:29:00.151
It's always haunted me.


00:29:01.820 --> 00:29:03.888
Is your husband here? Mm-hm.


00:29:03.890 --> 00:29:06.391
Can I talk to you both?


00:29:06.393 --> 00:29:08.359
Why?


00:29:08.361 --> 00:29:12.029
Anna just started to eat.


00:29:12.031 --> 00:29:14.132
So, will I see
you at 7:00 to celebrate?


00:29:14.134 --> 00:29:16.434
Okay, shall I pick you up then?


00:29:16.436 --> 00:29:18.403
Sure, why not?


00:29:18.405 --> 00:29:20.471
But only one drink.


00:29:50.536 --> 00:29:52.603
So you like being a nurse?


00:29:52.605 --> 00:29:54.338
I like helping people.


00:29:54.340 --> 00:29:56.808
You take your job quite
seriously, huh?


00:29:56.810 --> 00:30:00.511
Well, if you can't do what you
love, then at least make sure
you love what you do.


00:30:00.513 --> 00:30:02.013
Isn't that what they say?


00:30:02.015 --> 00:30:05.650
They do say that, that is
absolutely true.


00:30:08.387 --> 00:30:11.088
I think you're doing a
great job with Anna.


00:30:11.090 --> 00:30:14.425
Thank you for your confidence.


00:30:14.427 --> 00:30:17.628
Sometimes I don't think I'm
gonna be able to help her.


00:30:17.630 --> 00:30:19.197
Why?


00:30:21.733 --> 00:30:24.168
My wife and I had a baby boy...


00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:27.605
who died a few months
after he was born.


00:30:27.607 --> 00:30:34.612
My wife kept wanting to go back
to the time when he was
still alive, and...


00:30:34.614 --> 00:30:37.181
eventually the time came when...


00:30:37.183 --> 00:30:41.385
she wasn't happy unless she
was in the memory.


00:30:41.387 --> 00:30:43.488
She became obsessed.


00:30:43.490 --> 00:30:48.392
So, I refused to take her to
the past anymore.


00:30:48.394 --> 00:30:55.299
She... spiraled downward,
she... became depressed
and I lost her.


00:30:57.569 --> 00:31:00.638
I couldn't help her.


00:31:00.640 --> 00:31:05.877
I tried to keep her in the
house, but you can't
lock someone up...


00:31:05.879 --> 00:31:08.713
just because of your own fears.


00:31:20.392 --> 00:31:21.559
I had a great time.


00:31:21.561 --> 00:31:22.960
Me, too.


00:31:22.962 --> 00:31:25.496
I hope I didn't talk too much.
Oh, you did...


00:31:25.498 --> 00:31:27.298
but I liked it.


00:31:27.300 --> 00:31:29.166
Thank you.


00:31:29.168 --> 00:31:34.205
So, you're not even gonna try
to come up, so I can say no?


00:31:34.207 --> 00:31:36.007
Uh...


00:31:39.311 --> 00:31:42.313
I gotta go.


00:31:42.315 --> 00:31:44.148
Safe home.


00:31:52.658 --> 00:31:55.626
It's not
your fault, John!


00:31:58.163 --> 00:32:00.698
It's not
your fault, John!


00:32:09.509 --> 00:32:12.143
I'm telling you, Sebastian, I
saw her last night.


00:32:12.145 --> 00:32:14.412
That's impossible.


00:32:14.414 --> 00:32:17.014
<i>She's under lock and key, never
allowed to leave her room.</i>


00:32:17.016 --> 00:32:19.784
I know, but I... I
know what I saw.


00:32:19.786 --> 00:32:22.853
<i>Do you, John? Is
everything all right?</i>


00:32:22.855 --> 00:32:23.921
Everything's fine.


00:32:51.149 --> 00:32:55.052
We may have one, because
there are blind spots.


00:32:55.054 --> 00:32:56.954
What's happened?


00:32:56.956 --> 00:32:59.457
Anna pushed Judith
down the stairs.


00:32:59.459 --> 00:33:03.260
Judith is in the hospital with
multiple fractures.


00:33:04.796 --> 00:33:06.330
Look at this.


00:33:08.433 --> 00:33:12.370
Oh, my god!


00:33:12.372 --> 00:33:14.739
There's no other angle at the
top of the stairs?


00:33:14.741 --> 00:33:18.342
Blind spot.


00:33:18.344 --> 00:33:21.045
On Monday, Anna will be
confined to an institution...


00:33:21.047 --> 00:33:23.681
that can properly
address her needs.


00:33:23.683 --> 00:33:29.820
Fortunately, as a family
friend, Judith will not be
pressing any charges.


00:33:29.822 --> 00:33:31.856
I didn't do it, John.


00:33:31.858 --> 00:33:34.458
Then why would Judith
say you did?


00:33:34.460 --> 00:33:36.794
Judith always sneaks back
in late at night.


00:33:36.796 --> 00:33:40.064
Mom's knocked-out on sleeping
pills, and that's when
they have sex.


00:33:40.066 --> 00:33:43.300
Who? Robert and Judith?


00:33:43.302 --> 00:33:44.835
He always sleeps with the
good looking help.


00:33:44.837 --> 00:33:46.470
Just ask Jaime.


00:33:46.472 --> 00:33:48.305
I mean, you saw what she was
doing with Robert in
the library.


00:33:48.307 --> 00:33:51.942
I don't believe you.


00:33:51.944 --> 00:33:55.146
When she first came here,
Judith had tried to make
friends with me.


00:33:55.148 --> 00:33:56.981
And she was all like, "I have
no luck with men".


00:33:56.983 --> 00:33:58.482
Well, my stepfather
moved right in.


00:33:58.484 --> 00:34:00.718
You know, maybe... maybe they
had a fight, it got violent...


00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:02.687
and now they're trying to cover
it up by blaming it on
the sick girl.


00:34:02.689 --> 00:34:04.889
Or maybe Robert just
cold-bloodedly pushed her,
okay?


00:34:04.891 --> 00:34:07.892
This is exactly the kind of
thing he's been hoping
for to lock me up.


00:34:07.894 --> 00:34:09.193
Oh, c'mon, Anna.


00:34:09.195 --> 00:34:10.828
Open your eyes, John!


00:34:10.830 --> 00:34:14.131
My mother's family is one of
the richest in America.


00:34:14.133 --> 00:34:16.667
And Robert's on an allowance.


00:34:16.669 --> 00:34:21.172
If I die, the money goes to a
charitable trust and
he gets zilch.


00:34:21.174 --> 00:34:23.040
But if I'm committed...


00:34:23.042 --> 00:34:26.210
I get the money, but I
have no rights.


00:34:26.212 --> 00:34:28.279
Robert controls every penny.


00:34:28.281 --> 00:34:30.414
And I'm sure Judith knows this.


00:34:30.416 --> 00:34:34.018
Maybe he was afraid that she
was gonna tell you and that
you'd find out his
secret plans.


00:34:34.020 --> 00:34:37.521
And I'm sure he told you, only
moments ago, that they send me
to an institution on Monday.


00:34:37.523 --> 00:34:39.023
Am I right?


00:34:39.025 --> 00:34:42.359
Please, John, you have to help
me prove that I'm innocent.


00:34:42.361 --> 00:34:45.730
You're the only person
they're gonna trust.


00:34:45.732 --> 00:34:47.965
I... I can't get send away to a
mental institution.


00:34:47.967 --> 00:34:49.600
I won't survive that.


00:34:49.602 --> 00:34:52.403
I know... I know I'm different,
not like other girls...


00:34:52.405 --> 00:34:55.005
but doesn't mean I'm a murderer.


00:34:55.007 --> 00:34:58.175
I don't even... I don't even
think of doing half the things
they're accusing me of!


00:34:58.177 --> 00:34:59.910
Please, John!


00:34:59.912 --> 00:35:03.280
Help me figure out what the
hell's going on with me.


00:35:03.282 --> 00:35:05.583
I mean, you're all I have.


00:35:40.051 --> 00:35:41.652
John.


00:35:42.487 --> 00:35:44.555
How do you feel?


00:35:45.891 --> 00:35:48.459
Pretty out of it.


00:35:48.461 --> 00:35:53.464
Judith, did you see... Anna
push you down the stairs?


00:35:54.566 --> 00:35:56.834
Are you here for Anna or for me?


00:35:56.836 --> 00:35:59.336
I'm here for you.


00:35:59.338 --> 00:36:00.871
But I need to know
what happened.


00:36:02.340 --> 00:36:05.976
I know I went to bring
her some food.


00:36:07.779 --> 00:36:11.849
I thought I locked the door.


00:36:11.851 --> 00:36:14.885
Why don't you go to my memory?


00:36:17.289 --> 00:36:22.526
Ah... doesn't work like that.


00:36:22.528 --> 00:36:25.563
How do you know it
wasn't Robert?


00:36:25.565 --> 00:36:27.298
Robert?


00:36:28.166 --> 00:36:30.234
Judith, I know.


00:36:30.236 --> 00:36:32.970
Know what?


00:36:32.972 --> 00:36:36.273
I know about you and Robert.


00:36:36.275 --> 00:36:39.343
Did he hit on me?


00:36:41.313 --> 00:36:43.480
Whatever, doesn't matter.


00:36:43.482 --> 00:36:47.351
There's nothing going on
between me and Robert.


00:36:51.690 --> 00:36:54.325
Look, I...


00:36:56.461 --> 00:36:58.495
I hope you get better soon.


00:37:09.174 --> 00:37:11.942
I can't believe that Anna
would hurt Judith.


00:37:11.944 --> 00:37:14.111
Can you help my daughter, John?


00:37:14.113 --> 00:37:16.146
I believe I can, Mrs. Greene.


00:37:16.148 --> 00:37:20.217
I can take her to her traumatic
memories, help her
understand her behavior.


00:37:21.354 --> 00:37:22.887
And I wanna find out the truth.


00:37:22.889 --> 00:37:25.956
My husband wants to send her to
a professional care facility.


00:37:25.958 --> 00:37:28.826
I don't want that, but he's
already paid the
registration fee...


00:37:28.828 --> 00:37:30.828
and they're expecting
her in a week.


00:37:30.830 --> 00:37:35.799
As soon as I see that file,
I'll know what I should
be looking for.


00:37:35.801 --> 00:37:39.803
I'll have Sebastian's assistant
send it to you right away.


00:37:39.805 --> 00:37:42.106
Sebastian has it?


00:37:45.444 --> 00:37:49.046
<i>You'll
see why the family didn't want
you to see the file.</i>


00:37:49.048 --> 00:37:50.581
<i>It's strong stuff, John.</i>


00:37:50.583 --> 00:37:52.616
You said this was a simple case.


00:37:52.618 --> 00:37:54.551
<i>And it should have been, John.</i>


00:37:54.553 --> 00:37:57.021
Maybe you're not ready
to come back.


00:37:57.023 --> 00:37:59.723
Look... they're gonna put Anna
in an institution.


00:37:59.725 --> 00:38:03.260
If you'd sent me the file
earlier, maybe I could have
prevented all this.


00:38:03.262 --> 00:38:07.097
<i>Are you sure you want to
continue with the case?</i>


00:38:07.099 --> 00:38:09.166
I'm Anna's best hope right now.


00:38:09.168 --> 00:38:12.870
I'll call you in a
couple of days.


00:38:53.411 --> 00:38:55.846
<i>Do you know why you're here,
Anna?</i>


00:38:55.848 --> 00:38:58.115
That's pretty obvious.


00:38:58.117 --> 00:39:01.485
<i>For just one day, can we talk
about something other than me?</i>


00:39:01.487 --> 00:39:04.788
<i>What made you try to
kill yourself?</i>


00:39:04.790 --> 00:39:06.957
Red...


00:39:06.959 --> 00:39:09.560
<i>it's such a dark, rich color.</i>


00:39:09.562 --> 00:39:12.496
<i>Particular shade, it's
hard to come by.</i>


00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:17.935
<i>Blood... it's red.</i>


00:39:17.937 --> 00:39:19.570
It's kind of beautiful.


00:39:19.572 --> 00:39:22.773
<i>Can you tell me about your
relationship with your parents?</i>


00:39:22.775 --> 00:39:27.411
<i>My mother's trying harder, I
suppose, but it's still
pretty pathetic.</i>


00:39:27.413 --> 00:39:32.750
<i>Her heart's like... one of
those fancy ice sculptures
they have at parties.</i>


00:39:32.752 --> 00:39:36.387
<i>Do you really want to know
the answer? Please.</i>


00:39:36.389 --> 00:39:40.524
It's my parents who are
crazy... not me.


00:39:44.829 --> 00:39:49.600
<i>Did you have feelings for your
teacher? Mr. Tatum?</i>


00:39:49.602 --> 00:39:52.536
<i>That school was depressing.
He was nice.</i>


00:39:52.538 --> 00:39:54.538
Did he take pictures of you?


00:39:54.540 --> 00:39:55.906
<i>Would you
mind if I take a
picture of you?</i>


00:39:55.908 --> 00:39:57.141
<i>Yes.</i>


00:39:57.143 --> 00:39:59.276
<i>What kind of pictures?</i>


00:39:59.278 --> 00:40:01.612
Artistic photos.


00:40:08.386 --> 00:40:12.389
It was like a Jackson
Pollock painting...


00:40:12.391 --> 00:40:15.125
where the blood sprayed
across the floor.


00:40:18.029 --> 00:40:21.498
I can still see the exact
pattern when I close my eyes.


00:40:21.500 --> 00:40:24.401
<i>Do you want to die, Anna?</i>


00:40:24.403 --> 00:40:26.837
Don't we all die in the end?


00:40:28.273 --> 00:40:29.506
It's kind of a freedom.


00:40:29.508 --> 00:40:31.408
There are other ways to be free.


00:40:31.410 --> 00:40:34.278
Not if you're not
allowed to have it.


00:40:34.280 --> 00:40:36.914
Then what do you do?


00:41:01.739 --> 00:41:03.774
Will you lift your chin a bit?


00:41:08.613 --> 00:41:11.281
How do you feel when you draw?


00:41:11.283 --> 00:41:14.384
Like the whole world disappears.


00:41:14.386 --> 00:41:17.454
Like nothing else matters.


00:41:17.456 --> 00:41:19.356
All right, finished.


00:41:19.358 --> 00:41:20.390
Can I see it?


00:41:20.392 --> 00:41:24.428
Not yet.


00:41:24.430 --> 00:41:25.829
Can I have your bag?


00:41:32.971 --> 00:41:35.405
Promise me you'll look at it
when you get home?


00:41:35.407 --> 00:41:37.207
I promise.


00:41:37.209 --> 00:41:40.144
Are we even now?


00:41:40.146 --> 00:41:41.445
Can we start the session?


00:41:41.447 --> 00:41:43.780
Yeah, we can.


00:41:53.926 --> 00:41:56.260
Mousey? It's
extremely dangerous.


00:41:56.262 --> 00:41:58.162
My real name is Megan Scanlon.


00:41:58.164 --> 00:42:00.531
Had sex with your teacher?


00:42:00.533 --> 00:42:02.266
Who you raping ', bitch?


00:42:31.196 --> 00:42:33.797
Hi, I'm Mousey.


00:42:37.302 --> 00:42:40.337
Mousey? That's
really your name?


00:42:40.339 --> 00:42:41.872
It's what the people
here call me.


00:42:41.874 --> 00:42:45.509
My real name is Megan,
Megan Scanlon.


00:42:45.511 --> 00:42:47.277
So Susan Merricks your roommate.


00:42:47.279 --> 00:42:49.213
What's she really like?


00:42:49.215 --> 00:42:51.982
I heard she was training for
the Olympics, had a
nervous breakdown...


00:42:51.984 --> 00:42:53.817
beat up a
horse or something.


00:42:53.819 --> 00:42:58.121
Oh, great! Frigid and
Mousey are here.


00:42:58.123 --> 00:43:00.791
Look, just because I've been
assigned to watch over you...


00:43:00.793 --> 00:43:05.162
doesn't mean you have to be in
the room all the time, Frigid.


00:43:05.164 --> 00:43:06.597
Name's Anna.


00:43:06.599 --> 00:43:10.467
Capital A, N, N, A.


00:43:10.469 --> 00:43:14.004
Leave.


00:43:14.006 --> 00:43:15.339
Now.


00:43:20.044 --> 00:43:23.547
Or maybe the reason you won't
go is because you wanna
watch me changing.


00:43:23.549 --> 00:43:26.016
Right, Frigid?


00:43:29.954 --> 00:43:33.156
What are you doing? No! No! No!
Please don't!


00:43:33.158 --> 00:43:35.192
No! No! No! Stop!


00:43:40.232 --> 00:43:45.802
Cameras will be locked up, and
can only be signed out for
a day at a time.


00:43:50.041 --> 00:43:53.277
The chemicals you will be using
could be harmful...


00:43:53.279 --> 00:43:58.982
and any misuses, however
slight, will end your
art privileges.


00:43:58.984 --> 00:44:04.121
Now, who here has experience
with the art of photography?


00:44:32.884 --> 00:44:34.451
Anna.


00:44:34.453 --> 00:44:38.855
Someone broke into the
principal's house and stole
all the alcohol.


00:44:38.857 --> 00:44:40.857
Do you know who might
have done this?


00:44:57.642 --> 00:44:59.376
House Mother, you're
talking to someone...


00:44:59.378 --> 00:45:03.747
who takes the harmful effects
of alcohol very seriously.


00:45:03.749 --> 00:45:06.383
Drinking is the Devil's
calling card.


00:45:15.593 --> 00:45:18.428
Hey, Anna, look.


00:45:19.931 --> 00:45:22.599
I'm so, so sorry about
the closet. I...


00:45:22.601 --> 00:45:25.202
Oh, don't worry about it.


00:45:25.204 --> 00:45:29.539
Some friends are coming over to
tea tomorrow. Do you
want to join us?


00:45:29.541 --> 00:45:31.942
Can Megan come?


00:45:31.944 --> 00:45:35.278
What, Mousey? She's
such a retard.


00:45:35.280 --> 00:45:37.147
Yeah, she is.


00:45:53.865 --> 00:45:57.701
Do you copy your roses from the
rose bushes out there?


00:45:57.703 --> 00:46:00.237
Roses don't grow
during the winter.


00:46:02.573 --> 00:46:06.777
Sometimes we remember things
the way we want to, rather than
the way they really were.


00:46:06.779 --> 00:46:11.782
I didn't do anything to those
girls, if that's what
you're implying.


00:46:11.784 --> 00:46:17.421
False memories can have a... a
rushed feeling to them...


00:46:17.423 --> 00:46:19.356
a lack of detail.


00:46:19.358 --> 00:46:23.693
The windows won't have views or
none of the clocks will work.


00:46:23.695 --> 00:46:28.031
Well, if you ever find me, ah,
particularly attractive
in a memory...


00:46:28.033 --> 00:46:30.467
it's probably because I'm
making it up, too.


00:46:30.469 --> 00:46:34.337
I wouldn't picture myself
having a bad skin day if I
knew you'd be around.


00:46:34.339 --> 00:46:38.208
Hey, I'm not kidding, okay?


00:46:38.210 --> 00:46:40.610
I can accept we don't exactly
know what we're looking for...


00:46:40.612 --> 00:46:42.579
but your memories
have to be real!


00:46:42.581 --> 00:46:44.147
You have to be very careful!


00:46:44.149 --> 00:46:46.082
Has something told you I've
been making them up?


00:46:46.084 --> 00:46:49.886
Yeah, I saw a clock on the
wall, the hands weren't moving.


00:46:49.888 --> 00:46:52.589
The one in the dorm hallway,
right?


00:46:52.591 --> 00:46:54.391
Yeah.


00:46:54.393 --> 00:46:56.960
That one never worked.


00:46:56.962 --> 00:47:01.331
We used to call our gym
teacher, Mr. Pierce "The
Clock", because he didn't work,
either.


00:47:18.449 --> 00:47:20.884
You never leave the house,
right?


00:47:24.555 --> 00:47:26.289
Not anymore.


00:48:09.400 --> 00:48:11.635
You've got 20 minutes.


00:48:22.179 --> 00:48:24.347
Mr. Ortega?


00:48:24.349 --> 00:48:27.851
So, what are you? Some
kind of therapist?


00:48:27.853 --> 00:48:31.187
Do you know what a
memory detective is?


00:48:32.423 --> 00:48:35.292
Somebody who takes rich
people's money.


00:48:35.294 --> 00:48:37.160
Well, that's me.


00:48:37.162 --> 00:48:41.064
Has Anna's family hired you to
find out if she has a soul?


00:48:41.066 --> 00:48:43.500
I'm just here to find
out the truth.


00:48:43.502 --> 00:48:47.070
That family is a nightmare.


00:48:47.072 --> 00:48:49.806
You dig too deep, better
watch your step.


00:48:49.808 --> 00:48:53.243
You're lucky you didn't get 20
years for seducing a minor.


00:48:53.245 --> 00:48:58.114
I'm not saying I wasn't at
fault, but that girl...


00:48:58.116 --> 00:49:04.120
that girl was everywhere I
turned... flirting...


00:49:04.122 --> 00:49:09.926
finding ways to get us alone.


00:49:09.928 --> 00:49:12.162
I've lost everything.


00:49:13.831 --> 00:49:17.200
My job, my fiance, my freedom...


00:49:17.202 --> 00:49:22.339
my entire fucking life,
because of her.


00:49:22.341 --> 00:49:25.675
Anna's family throws money
around like confetti.


00:49:25.677 --> 00:49:27.844
They can get to anybody.


00:49:27.846 --> 00:49:31.014
Cops, district attorneys...


00:49:31.016 --> 00:49:34.584
They've covered up all the bad
stuff Anna's done.


00:49:34.586 --> 00:49:38.855
Then, had me thrown in here for
something I didn't do.


00:49:38.857 --> 00:49:43.126
I'm sure that they even covered
it up when she tried to kill...


00:49:43.128 --> 00:49:46.363
those three girls at school
that same year.


00:49:46.365 --> 00:49:49.633
Anna blamed it all on
another girl, Mousey...


00:49:49.635 --> 00:49:52.636
but no one could find
out who she was.


00:49:52.638 --> 00:49:58.274
Not even Susan Merrick s family
was able to take Anna to court.


00:49:58.276 --> 00:50:02.579
I'd love that family to finally
get what's coming to them.


00:50:25.002 --> 00:50:27.070
Susan Merrick?


00:50:29.640 --> 00:50:33.943
My name is John Washington. Can
I ask you a few questions
about Anna Greene?


00:50:33.945 --> 00:50:37.747
Are you a cop?


00:50:37.749 --> 00:50:39.949
No, I'm not a cop, Ms. Merrick.


00:50:39.951 --> 00:50:41.685
What? Has she died
or something?


00:50:41.687 --> 00:50:43.853
No... not at all.


00:50:43.855 --> 00:50:49.025
I just want to find out what
happened, what really happened
at the Whitten Academy.


00:50:49.027 --> 00:50:51.695
You think Anna was responsible.


00:50:51.697 --> 00:50:55.065
Of course, she was a
total psycho.


00:50:55.067 --> 00:50:58.802
There were a lot of other girls
there with problems. Could
have been anyone.


00:50:58.804 --> 00:51:01.104
I got on with everyone.


00:51:01.106 --> 00:51:04.874
Did you have a girl named
Mousey at your school?


00:51:04.876 --> 00:51:08.912
No... I don't think so.


00:51:08.914 --> 00:51:10.513
Now, I'm sorry, but
I have to go.


00:51:10.515 --> 00:51:12.582
Miss Merrick, I know what
you've been through.


00:51:13.918 --> 00:51:16.453
I know it must have been
extremely painful.


00:51:16.455 --> 00:51:19.756
I really need your help.


00:51:19.758 --> 00:51:23.326
Do you have any specific memory
of Anna you think I
should know?


00:51:25.129 --> 00:51:28.698
Yeah... sure I do.


00:52:03.300 --> 00:52:08.438
Anna seriously has balls. She
was like "drinking is the
Devil's calling card".


00:52:08.440 --> 00:52:10.273
It was awesome.


00:52:13.677 --> 00:52:17.947
Hey, Anna, do you want a cup?


00:52:17.949 --> 00:52:19.349
No, thanks.


00:52:19.351 --> 00:52:20.884
You sure?


00:52:20.886 --> 00:52:23.253
Yeah.


00:52:29.660 --> 00:52:31.394
I like you being here with us.


00:53:24.014 --> 00:53:27.350
And coming back... now.


00:53:37.494 --> 00:53:41.965
You saw Mousey,
right? She did it.


00:53:41.967 --> 00:53:44.567
So you didn't poison
those girls?


00:53:44.569 --> 00:53:46.302
Of course, not.


00:53:47.471 --> 00:53:50.340
Your prints were all
over the teapot.


00:53:50.342 --> 00:53:52.775
Because I picked it up
once or twice.


00:53:52.777 --> 00:53:56.145
And why would I wipe the poison
clean, but leave my
prints on the teapot?


00:53:56.147 --> 00:53:59.549
Not to mention hiding the
poison under my bed.


00:53:59.551 --> 00:54:02.252
Maybe you're too smart
for your own good.


00:54:02.254 --> 00:54:04.254
If you'd wiped the pot, that
would point to you.


00:54:04.256 --> 00:54:08.191
Maybe you just didn't have time
to hide the poison.


00:54:08.193 --> 00:54:10.260
It was Megan, John.


00:54:11.262 --> 00:54:13.329
Why didn't you go to the cops?


00:54:13.331 --> 00:54:17.100
What, and tell them that Megan
was obsessed and that she
smirked at me as I
was led away?


00:54:17.102 --> 00:54:18.768
Why not?


00:54:18.770 --> 00:54:21.271
You're forgetting what it's
like to be a teenager.


00:54:21.273 --> 00:54:25.541
Adults telling you what to do,
having opinion about what you
say, before you even say it.


00:54:25.543 --> 00:54:29.445
There's no Mousey, Anna. What?


00:54:29.447 --> 00:54:30.580
What are you talking about?


00:54:30.582 --> 00:54:32.148
There's no Megan at the school.


00:54:32.150 --> 00:54:34.918
Oh, you don't believe me?
Do you blame me?


00:54:34.920 --> 00:54:40.256
Megan transferred in during the
second semester and left right
after I got expelled.


00:54:40.258 --> 00:54:41.658
You know, who the hell do
you think I am?


00:54:41.660 --> 00:54:43.126
Please tell me, John!


00:54:43.128 --> 00:54:44.861
What... what, you think I'm
some psychopath?


00:54:44.863 --> 00:54:47.563
What? This is the second day in
a row you've called me a liar!


00:54:47.565 --> 00:54:50.300
I want to know why you're
suddenly turning on me!


00:54:51.602 --> 00:54:54.203
Here! My yearbook!


00:54:54.205 --> 00:54:55.705
Asshole.


00:55:10.487 --> 00:55:13.423
You won't mind if I hang on to
this for a couple of days?


00:55:13.425 --> 00:55:16.192
Sleep with it under your
pillow, for all I care.


00:55:16.194 --> 00:55:18.027
We don't have much time.


00:55:18.029 --> 00:55:22.732
I want you to think about all
the key moments in your
life by tomorrow.


00:55:22.734 --> 00:55:24.434
Can you do that for me?


00:55:25.436 --> 00:55:26.769
Fine.


00:56:34.873 --> 00:56:36.572
John...


00:56:36.574 --> 00:56:38.474
John, Why don't you help me?


00:56:38.476 --> 00:56:40.843
Why don't you wanna help me?


00:56:40.845 --> 00:56:42.445
Mom!


00:56:44.082 --> 00:56:50.586
This old man,
he played three.


00:56:50.588 --> 00:56:54.490
He played
knick-knack on my knee.


00:56:54.492 --> 00:56:56.492
With a knick-knack
paddy whack...


00:56:56.494 --> 00:56:58.961
give a dog a bone, this old...


00:56:58.963 --> 00:57:01.397
Who's there?


00:57:23.954 --> 00:57:25.088
Anna?


00:57:28.692 --> 00:57:30.026
Anna!


00:57:37.235 --> 00:57:38.835
Hello?


00:58:34.791 --> 00:58:38.094
Hey!


00:58:38.096 --> 00:58:39.428
Wait!


00:58:51.175 --> 00:58:53.476
Wait!


00:59:16.500 --> 00:59:18.167
Is there somewhere I
can freshen up?


00:59:18.169 --> 00:59:21.304
There's a bathroom just down
that corridor on your left.


00:59:21.306 --> 00:59:22.905
Oh, thank you.


01:01:05.375 --> 01:01:09.712
What are you doing in here?


01:01:09.714 --> 01:01:12.315
Maybe I'm looking for the
guy from last night.


01:01:15.018 --> 01:01:20.389
You know, Mr. Greene, it really
isn't necessary to
have me followed.


01:01:20.391 --> 01:01:23.659
I had you extensively looked
into before you were hired.


01:01:23.661 --> 01:01:26.262
I don't have anyone
following you now.


01:01:26.264 --> 01:01:30.966
And now, if you'd be so kind,
your work in this
house is upstairs.


01:02:27.324 --> 01:02:29.158
Very nice, Anna.


01:02:31.661 --> 01:02:34.830
Not just yet.


01:03:17.908 --> 01:03:20.776
Glad you're back from
zombie land.


01:03:20.778 --> 01:03:23.345
You okay, want some water?


01:03:27.951 --> 01:03:31.754
Aren't they great? Better than
what you had before.


01:03:33.056 --> 01:03:34.590
How did you do that?


01:03:34.592 --> 01:03:36.859
I just downloaded it.


01:03:36.861 --> 01:03:39.161
No, how did you leave me
alone in the memory?


01:03:39.163 --> 01:03:41.363
I don't know.


01:03:41.365 --> 01:03:45.835
Suddenly I was back here, and
our hands were separated, but
you were still under.


01:03:45.837 --> 01:03:48.270
I wasn't sure what to do.


01:03:52.843 --> 01:03:55.377
You looked cute while you
were sleeping.


01:04:04.855 --> 01:04:08.224
Anna, do you know what
transference is?


01:04:09.292 --> 01:04:10.860
I do.


01:04:10.862 --> 01:04:12.962
Then you'll know it's
perfectly natural to...


01:04:12.964 --> 01:04:16.632
To what? Have strong feelings
for your therapist?


01:04:16.634 --> 01:04:19.735
I just simply said I liked
watching you sleep.


01:04:21.204 --> 01:04:23.973
Your teacher was a lot older
than you, he took advantage.


01:04:23.975 --> 01:04:28.143
He was encouraging... that
place was so depressing.


01:04:28.145 --> 01:04:30.179
What about the photos?


01:04:30.181 --> 01:04:33.883
He said they were for art, and
at first they were artistic.


01:06:07.911 --> 01:06:09.678
You okay? You don't
look too good.


01:06:09.680 --> 01:06:12.114
I'm having trouble
staying grounded.


01:06:12.116 --> 01:06:14.683
Side-effects from the sessions?
Hallucinations?


01:06:14.685 --> 01:06:16.051
Yeah... terrible headaches.


01:06:16.053 --> 01:06:18.354
I can't sleep... nightmares.


01:06:18.356 --> 01:06:19.989
Plus the guy they've hired
to follow me...


01:06:19.991 --> 01:06:21.991
he's... he is everywhere I go.


01:06:21.993 --> 01:06:27.696
Maybe events have made this
case far bigger than you were
ready for when you started.


01:06:27.698 --> 01:06:29.798
Maybe we should ask
Lundgren to take over.


01:06:29.800 --> 01:06:33.002
No! No way, no. I
can handle it.


01:06:35.572 --> 01:06:38.374
Did you ever treat Anna
at their house?


01:06:38.376 --> 01:06:39.708
No.


01:06:39.710 --> 01:06:42.911
Did you ever have reason to
suspect abuse
within the family?


01:06:42.913 --> 01:06:44.446
Nothing with the stepfather?


01:06:44.448 --> 01:06:48.283
Highly unlikely. I mean, look,
Robert's a prominent guy.


01:06:48.285 --> 01:06:51.620
I wouldn't go down that road
based on a hunch.


01:06:51.622 --> 01:06:54.456
Tom Ortega told me Anna's
parents set him up for...


01:06:54.458 --> 01:06:57.226
You went to see Tom Ortega?


01:06:57.228 --> 01:06:59.995
That lowlife took dirty
pictures of Anna.


01:06:59.997 --> 01:07:03.165
You should be focusing on the
sessions, not investigating
in the real world.


01:07:03.167 --> 01:07:04.933
You need to be objective, John.


01:07:04.935 --> 01:07:08.904
There is something going on
there behind the scenes...


01:07:08.906 --> 01:07:10.572
I need to find out what it is.


01:07:10.574 --> 01:07:13.909
You need to consider that this
job is too big and
too complex...


01:07:13.911 --> 01:07:16.311
and that you are becoming too
personally involved.


01:07:16.313 --> 01:07:19.314
Whatever it is, I'm gonna
find out the truth.


01:07:48.111 --> 01:07:50.446
Do you know where
you want to go?


01:07:50.448 --> 01:07:55.250
I went through all the photos
and one of them made me
feel something.


01:07:55.252 --> 01:07:56.452
Don't tell me.


01:07:56.454 --> 01:07:58.921
Don't corrupt the memory,
just go there.


01:08:03.359 --> 01:08:07.229
When you're ready,
close your eyes.


01:08:09.432 --> 01:08:13.335
Let's begin... now.


01:08:18.108 --> 01:08:20.843
My parents brought him to me.
Who?


01:08:20.845 --> 01:08:22.511
I don't remember his name.


01:08:31.955 --> 01:08:35.324
This old man, he played three.


01:08:35.326 --> 01:08:38.260
He played
knick-knack on my knee.


01:08:38.262 --> 01:08:42.631
With a knick-knack paddy whack,
give a dog a bone.


01:08:42.633 --> 01:08:46.802
This old man came rolling home.


01:09:08.858 --> 01:09:11.393
What are you doing over there,
Anna?


01:09:12.996 --> 01:09:16.999
Why don't you come here...
next to me.


01:09:18.535 --> 01:09:21.336
Come here, sweetheart.


01:09:31.948 --> 01:09:33.148
Don't be afraid.


01:09:35.119 --> 01:09:39.087
I won't hurt you.


01:09:39.089 --> 01:09:41.323
And coming back... now!


01:09:46.362 --> 01:09:47.663
Anna?


01:09:49.066 --> 01:09:50.399
Anna, can you hear me?


01:09:51.635 --> 01:09:52.768
You're okay, you fainted.


01:09:52.770 --> 01:09:54.036
What happened?


01:09:54.038 --> 01:09:56.471
Can you get some water.
She's okay.


01:09:56.473 --> 01:09:59.107
Yeah, sure.


01:10:02.812 --> 01:10:04.746
Take this.


01:10:04.748 --> 01:10:06.815
What is it?


01:10:06.817 --> 01:10:11.153
It's a bit of one of your mom's
sedatives. It'll
help you sleep.


01:10:18.161 --> 01:10:20.462
So, what happens now?


01:10:20.464 --> 01:10:24.800
Now... you get better.


01:10:41.618 --> 01:10:46.255
This is the key to the house my
parents lived in
when I was born.


01:10:46.257 --> 01:10:49.157
I always felt safe there.


01:10:49.159 --> 01:10:51.994
So many times in my life
people have been unkind.


01:10:51.996 --> 01:10:55.864
I can't thank you enough, John.


01:10:55.866 --> 01:10:59.801
Will you keep this with
you at all times?


01:10:59.803 --> 01:11:02.905
If I know you have it, then at
least I know that there's
someone out there...


01:11:02.907 --> 01:11:04.573
who's on my side.


01:11:04.575 --> 01:11:07.876
I might not be going to
an institution...


01:11:07.878 --> 01:11:10.779
but I still feel trapped.


01:11:10.781 --> 01:11:12.347
Sure.


01:11:29.532 --> 01:11:32.301
Hey! Hey!


01:11:35.872 --> 01:11:37.272
John? What are you doing here?


01:11:37.274 --> 01:11:39.074
You should have called, I've
got dinner guests.


01:11:39.076 --> 01:11:40.909
Why Sebastian?


01:11:40.911 --> 01:11:43.045
Christ! She was just a child.


01:11:43.047 --> 01:11:45.314
What's going on? You've
been drinking?


01:11:46.449 --> 01:11:49.284
These were in Anna's memories.


01:11:49.286 --> 01:11:51.520
Have you been in my office?


01:11:51.522 --> 01:11:55.624
I've seen you with her, in the
library, in one of
the memories.


01:11:55.626 --> 01:11:57.993
Oh, I might have been there
once, I forgot!


01:11:57.995 --> 01:11:59.895
What's this all about?


01:11:59.897 --> 01:12:03.465
You said you never treated her
at the house, but
you were there!


01:12:05.068 --> 01:12:08.003
Are you trying to say I did
something to her?


01:12:08.005 --> 01:12:10.005
Think this through, John.


01:12:10.007 --> 01:12:15.210
Why would I ask you to take on
a case, if I was guilty
of something?


01:12:15.212 --> 01:12:17.412
Think about what it is you're
accusing me of...


01:12:17.414 --> 01:12:21.350
then, think about who it is
you're accusing.


01:12:21.352 --> 01:12:23.352
They wanted to hire
Peter Lundgren.


01:12:23.354 --> 01:12:26.488
You brought me in, because I
was down, and I was weak...


01:12:26.490 --> 01:12:29.591
and I was easy to manipulate.
Right?


01:12:29.593 --> 01:12:33.095
And you wouldn't let me see
that file until you
absolutely had to.


01:12:33.097 --> 01:12:36.298
You said they didn't want me to
see it, but you had it
the whole time!


01:12:36.300 --> 01:12:38.533
I never told you I didn't
have the file!


01:12:38.535 --> 01:12:41.703
I said the family
wanted privacy.


01:12:41.705 --> 01:12:44.339
What about the other day? Ah?
You wanted me to drop the case.


01:12:44.341 --> 01:12:45.941
I said that because...


01:12:45.943 --> 01:12:48.543
Now... I know what you didn't
want me to find out.


01:12:48.545 --> 01:12:51.046
I said that because I was
worried about you!


01:12:51.048 --> 01:12:54.483
Oh, c'mon, John!


01:12:54.485 --> 01:12:57.452
You've been drinking alone.
Having hallucinations for days!


01:12:57.454 --> 01:12:59.788
You're ignoring me again,
Uncle Sebastian


01:12:59.790 --> 01:13:01.390
Hi, sweetheart.


01:13:02.558 --> 01:13:05.227
Sorry. John...


01:13:05.229 --> 01:13:09.798
Don't you ever go near Anna
again! You hear me?


01:13:12.935 --> 01:13:15.637
John!


01:13:15.639 --> 01:13:16.905
John!


01:13:20.476 --> 01:13:23.745
Due to Anna's
early overt sexualization...


01:13:23.747 --> 01:13:25.380
she has a need for control...


01:13:25.382 --> 01:13:28.984
which manifests itself in a
variety of disorders.


01:13:28.986 --> 01:13:31.586
She has... significant
difficulty...


01:13:31.588 --> 01:13:36.425
in forming and maintaining
long-term
relationships with others.


01:13:36.427 --> 01:13:38.760
Basically, she has developed a
protective shell...


01:13:38.762 --> 01:13:40.262
Do you like it? which keeps
out the pain...


01:13:40.264 --> 01:13:43.932
and keeps out everything else.
It's great.


01:13:43.934 --> 01:13:47.536
She interacts with the world in
a completely different way
than the way we do.


01:13:47.538 --> 01:13:50.772
Locking her up is the worst
possible thing you could do.


01:13:56.646 --> 01:14:00.649
Thank you so much, Mr.
Washington.


01:14:00.651 --> 01:14:02.684
Good luck.


01:15:06.616 --> 01:15:09.885
<i>It's not
your fault, John.</i>


01:15:12.989 --> 01:15:15.824
<i>This
person... they lied
about everything.</i>


01:15:15.826 --> 01:15:19.594
<i>But just because the lies are
shocking and they attract a
lot of attention...</i>


01:15:19.596 --> 01:15:22.297
it doesn't necessarily
make them true.


01:15:22.299 --> 01:15:24.666
It was very important
for us to...


01:15:24.668 --> 01:15:27.269
<i>to check the facts and to
question the facts...</i>


01:15:27.271 --> 01:15:29.604
until it was evident that
I was innocent.


01:15:29.606 --> 01:15:33.642
<i>And once we've proven my
innocence, we went back
to that proof...</i>


01:15:33.644 --> 01:15:37.078
<i>over and over again, and looked
at it with a fresh set of eyes.</i>


01:15:37.080 --> 01:15:41.449
<i>Because only then, were we able
to actually see the truth.</i>


01:15:41.451 --> 01:15:43.952
<i>Are there any questions?</i>


01:15:43.954 --> 01:15:45.720
How does it
feel to be designated?


01:15:45.722 --> 01:15:47.489
<i>That's a
good question...</i>


01:15:47.491 --> 01:15:49.024
<i>and I just want to thank my
constituency...</i>


01:17:06.535 --> 01:17:09.704
I just
downloaded it.


01:17:09.706 --> 01:17:12.474
Aren't they great? Better than
what you had before.


01:17:49.579 --> 01:17:52.013
<i>Hello?
Can you come over?</i>


01:17:52.015 --> 01:17:53.214
I need to see you, John.


01:17:53.216 --> 01:17:54.382
Anna, look, I need to talk to...


01:17:54.384 --> 01:17:56.318
Before it's too late!


01:17:56.320 --> 01:17:58.320
<i>Something terrible has
happened and I need to...</i>


01:17:58.322 --> 01:18:02.691
What? Hello?


01:18:02.693 --> 01:18:04.993
Hello?


01:18:08.865 --> 01:18:11.032
<i>You have
reached the Greene's residence.</i>


01:18:11.034 --> 01:18:14.169
<i>Please leave a message and
we'll get back to you as
soon as we can.</i>


01:18:56.513 --> 01:18:59.614
Hello?


01:19:37.486 --> 01:19:40.255
<i>Anna?
John.</i>


01:20:25.969 --> 01:20:28.069
Hey!


01:20:28.071 --> 01:20:30.004
Open the door!


01:20:30.006 --> 01:20:34.209
<i>John, there's
someone in our house!</i>


01:20:41.650 --> 01:20:44.853
Shit!


01:20:44.855 --> 01:20:48.256
Mom? Mom?


01:20:48.258 --> 01:20:49.557
Hello?


01:20:49.559 --> 01:20:50.692
<i>Wh... emergency...</i>


01:20:50.694 --> 01:20:51.826
Hello, can you hear me?


01:20:56.232 --> 01:20:57.732
Shit.


01:20:57.734 --> 01:20:59.254
- I
- don't want to die!


01:21:17.353 --> 01:21:22.190
Hey! Hey! Open the
goddamn door!


01:22:07.671 --> 01:22:10.104
<i>911,
what's your emergency?</i>


01:22:10.106 --> 01:22:13.441
I'm at 1103 Bayside.


01:22:13.443 --> 01:22:17.779
I have an intruder and a
serious assault.


01:22:17.781 --> 01:22:19.447
Okay, that's right.


01:22:19.449 --> 01:22:22.550
We already have multiple units
responding to that address,
sir.


01:22:44.239 --> 01:22:45.373
Anna!


01:22:47.109 --> 01:22:48.876
Wait!


01:23:01.624 --> 01:23:03.891
Anna!


01:23:19.174 --> 01:23:21.676
John.


01:23:21.678 --> 01:23:26.114
Anna! You okay? You hurt?


01:23:29.351 --> 01:23:31.185
Look, we're being followed...


01:23:31.187 --> 01:23:35.723
but the police are here, you
stay with me you're gonna
be safe. Okay?


01:23:39.228 --> 01:23:41.062
I'm sorry.


01:23:43.832 --> 01:23:44.832
What?


01:23:45.935 --> 01:23:48.102
There's something over there!


01:23:52.608 --> 01:23:56.344
Hey! Hey!


01:23:56.346 --> 01:23:58.046
Over here!


01:24:03.385 --> 01:24:04.986
Hey! Stop!
Stop!


01:24:04.988 --> 01:24:06.988
Hey! Somebody's broken into
the Greene's house!


01:24:06.990 --> 01:24:08.556
Police! I'm pretty su...


01:24:08.558 --> 01:24:10.291
Stay where you are! Stay
right where you are!


01:24:10.293 --> 01:24:16.030
Hands up, Mr. Washington! Hands
up, Mr. Washington!


01:24:45.394 --> 01:24:48.796
You're
suspected of murder, Mr.
Washington.


01:24:52.134 --> 01:24:55.536
We found hundreds of pictures
featuring underage girls...


01:24:55.538 --> 01:24:58.239
in your computer.


01:24:58.241 --> 01:24:59.741
She set me up.


01:24:59.743 --> 01:25:04.545
A 16 year-old girl.


01:25:04.547 --> 01:25:09.784
Look. We know the parents were
constantly threatening to send
the girl to an institution...


01:25:09.786 --> 01:25:12.053
and that you... strongly
disagreed with that.


01:25:12.055 --> 01:25:15.289
So the way I see it, you got
too close to the girl.


01:25:15.291 --> 01:25:17.792
You drugged the parents, so you
could take her away...


01:25:17.794 --> 01:25:22.930
but she refused to go and you
end up doing something you'd
never think you
were capable of.


01:25:22.932 --> 01:25:24.732
The parents are okay?


01:25:24.734 --> 01:25:29.904
Yeah... we found the mother's
sleeping pills in the kitchen,
John.


01:25:29.906 --> 01:25:34.942
And I'd be willing to bet that
your fingerprints are all over
that prescription bottle.


01:25:34.944 --> 01:25:37.645
We found a letter opener,
covered in blood...


01:25:37.647 --> 01:25:40.948
in the forest, where you were.


01:25:40.950 --> 01:25:43.684
I can explain every peace of
evidence you think you have.


01:25:43.686 --> 01:25:49.090
We're carefully going through
the tapes of you chasing Anna.


01:25:49.092 --> 01:25:51.025
Now obviously you disabled a
number of the cameras...


01:25:51.027 --> 01:25:53.628
and then turned the power off
to cover your tracks.


01:25:53.630 --> 01:25:57.965
I was locked inside the
surveillance room!


01:26:02.604 --> 01:26:04.605
Recognize this?


01:26:06.308 --> 01:26:08.109
Anna gave me that.


01:26:11.280 --> 01:26:15.449
It's the key to the
surveillance room.


01:26:16.919 --> 01:26:19.387
You panicked, needed an alibi...


01:26:19.389 --> 01:26:23.858
so you damaged the interior of
the door, but you forgot...


01:26:23.860 --> 01:26:28.496
that you had the key
in your pocket.


01:26:28.498 --> 01:26:31.098
Do the right thing, John...


01:26:31.100 --> 01:26:34.068
and tell me what you did
with the girl.


01:26:34.070 --> 01:26:37.772
I went to the house, I was
looking for her.


01:26:37.774 --> 01:26:40.174
And you got locked in the
surveillance room.


01:26:40.176 --> 01:26:43.077
Exactly. And when I got out,
it was too late.


01:26:43.079 --> 01:26:48.049
And there was blood on the
floor in the hallway, I
followed the trail
to the forest!


01:26:48.051 --> 01:26:50.251
And that's how you got the
blood on your shoes? Yes.


01:26:50.253 --> 01:26:55.122
By following the trail of blood
from a 16 year-old... in a
massive forest.


01:26:55.124 --> 01:26:59.627
Yes, and... she came
out of nowhere.


01:26:59.629 --> 01:27:05.967
She... she grabbed my hands, my
hands had blood on them.


01:27:05.969 --> 01:27:09.370
She ran away.


01:27:09.372 --> 01:27:12.173
And was this before or after
she called 911 on her cell...


01:27:12.175 --> 01:27:17.378
screaming and crying that you
were chasing her through the
house, trying to kill her?


01:27:17.380 --> 01:27:19.680
There is plenty of evidence
to convict you.


01:27:19.682 --> 01:27:23.684
There was someone else there.


01:27:23.686 --> 01:27:26.454
You're gonna die in jail.


01:27:40.970 --> 01:27:44.906
And coming back... now.


01:28:07.729 --> 01:28:11.599
<i>End of move,
end of move!</i>


01:28:18.106 --> 01:28:19.573
Okay, that's it.


01:28:19.575 --> 01:28:22.543
We visited all the necessary
memories together...


01:28:22.545 --> 01:28:27.515
through every aspect of your
involvement in Anna's case.


01:28:27.517 --> 01:28:30.251
I should have realized
what she was doing.


01:28:30.253 --> 01:28:32.520
It's not your fault, John.


01:28:32.522 --> 01:28:35.923
Anna was able to study our
protocols during your
time with her...


01:28:35.925 --> 01:28:39.727
and she eventually became
strong enough to control and
manipulate the sessions.


01:28:39.729 --> 01:28:46.167
She was even able to figure out
that water triggered the
memories of your
wife's suicide.


01:28:46.169 --> 01:28:48.569
She needed you to be
responsible for her death.


01:28:48.571 --> 01:28:53.407
If she just ran away, her
parents would just keep
searching for her.


01:28:53.409 --> 01:28:56.077
Did you find anything?


01:28:56.079 --> 01:28:58.179
I'll submit our sessions
to the judge...


01:28:58.181 --> 01:29:01.415
specifically highlighting the
time you were locked in the
surveillance room...


01:29:01.417 --> 01:29:03.584
and when you spoke to her
in the forest...


01:29:03.586 --> 01:29:07.488
but as you know, our sessions
don't yet carry the
same weight...


01:29:07.490 --> 01:29:09.991
as eye witness
testimony in court.


01:29:09.993 --> 01:29:14.562
The only irrefutable evidence
you could have is proving
Anna's still out there...


01:29:14.564 --> 01:29:18.532
but... that's something
beyond my capabilities.


01:29:20.603 --> 01:29:23.137
Mr. Lundgren?


01:29:45.694 --> 01:29:48.229
I'm so sorry.


01:29:48.231 --> 01:29:52.166
I don't know how she made
me believe her.


01:29:52.168 --> 01:29:54.668
She had me completely fooled.


01:29:58.240 --> 01:30:00.508
It's all good, John.


01:30:00.510 --> 01:30:03.477
You've been under a lot of
pressure lately.


01:30:03.479 --> 01:30:05.279
Thank you.


01:30:05.281 --> 01:30:09.417
The judge is gonna consider
Peter's testimony for sure...


01:30:09.419 --> 01:30:11.552
but since you both work
for Mindscape...


01:30:11.554 --> 01:30:15.556
there are some legal issues we
need to get over and
that'll take time.


01:30:15.558 --> 01:30:16.824
I know.


01:30:16.826 --> 01:30:20.227
Now... the sooner you get rid
of the house the better.


01:30:20.229 --> 01:30:23.464
It won't take long before the
bail will be granted.


01:30:23.466 --> 01:30:26.767
But don't worry, John,
you're not alone.


01:30:26.769 --> 01:30:30.871
I'm gonna do everything in my
power to help you get
clear of this.


01:31:05.774 --> 01:31:09.310
And you just
want to send a single rose?


01:31:09.312 --> 01:31:13.747
A single rose and...
this photograph.


01:31:17.819 --> 01:31:21.989
Would you be so kind as to
remove all the thorns,
before sending it over?


01:31:21.991 --> 01:31:24.825
You can count on it, yeah.


01:31:44.045 --> 01:31:46.113
<i>The funny
thing about memory...</i>


01:31:46.115 --> 01:31:48.849
is that it can't be
fully trusted.


01:31:55.857 --> 01:32:01.929
<i>And yet, in the end, it's the
only truth we have.</i>


01:32:01.931 --> 01:32:07.134
<i>And no matter how painful it
is, you gotta look at
the truth...</i>


01:32:07.136 --> 01:32:09.503
because sometimes...


01:32:09.505 --> 01:32:12.606
it's the only thing
that can save you.


01:32:15.877 --> 01:32:18.112
It's the only thing...


01:32:18.114 --> 01:32:21.248
that can set you free.


01:32:39.901 --> 01:32:42.937
I just thought I'd...


01:32:42.939 --> 01:32:45.472
try to come up so you
could say no.


01:32:47.142 --> 01:32:49.210
Come in.

